        "description": "<div id=\"remove_no_follow\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid grid--cols-10@md grid--cols-8@lg article-column\">\n\t\t\t\t\t  <div class=\"col-12 col-10@md col-6@lg col-start-3@lg\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"article-column__content\">\n<section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you like audiobooks but don\u2019t want to be tied down to Audible, there are actually some good free alternatives out there. Two that I recommend are Audiobookshelf and Storyteller. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both are self-hosted, which means that your library stays on your own computer or server, rather than in a company\u2019s cloud. The only catch being that you need to own your audiobooks to use them\u2014something that isn\u2019t possible if you\u2019re switching directly from Audible.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Both are perfectly fine Audible audiobook listening alternatives, but they have slightly unique features that set them apart from one another.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 ",
